  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support Composting by Women in Kibera, Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Advocacy Project is seeking $2,000 to help Shield of Faith, a dynamic woman&apos;s association, use vermiculture as a way to improve nutrition and reduce pollution in Kibera. Led by their inspiring coordinator Stella, seen in the photo, the group has set ambitious goals for this year: compost 500 kilos of food waste; grow a third of their vegetables in kitchen gardens; and sell 50 liters of leachate (fertilizer) produced by their worms. They feel this will inspire others to change their behavior.</narrative>
  </description>
